    <sys:String x:Key="Handle.Title">HandleScope integration</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Handle.Heading">HandleScope integration</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Handle.Detail">Install and connect SessionDock to the optional local HandleScope API.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Handle.CheckingSetup">Checking local setup...</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Handle.CheckingDetail">SessionDock is inspecting local files only.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Handle.Attention">Configuration needs attention</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Handle.AttentionDetail">SessionDock preserved the existing configuration and will not use it. Repair replaces only the SessionDock opt-in with the fixed, minimal Roblox policy; it does not reinstall or stop HandleScope.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Handle.Controls">SETUP AND CONTROLS</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Handle.SecurityDetail">The install button contacts only the canonical immutable HandleScope GitHub release. SessionDock verifies exact asset sizes and hashes, the matching checksum, safe ZIP layout, every internal file, and the installed API hash before trusting it. HandleScope is unsigned, so these checks confirm the GitHub release rather than a certificate-backed publisher. Installation starts the API now and enables its limited per-user autostart at Windows sign-in; it never elevates or changes SessionDock's integration setting.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Handle.InstallTooltip">Download, verify, and install the latest stable HandleScope release for this Windows user</sys:String>
